Design for Product Interoperability is a strategy that drives improvements in independent maintenance of the product by users, to extend the product lifecycle of it. The ultimate goal of the strategy is to create a product system that can empower the users to address their unique needs by enabling them to access, exchange, integrate, repair, disassemble, reassemble and cooperatively use and understand a product. The ultimate goal for a company that wants to use this strategy is to create an easy and well-connected system that can empower the users to address their unique needs. Achieving this goal requires a more detailed understanding of both those who use the product and those who provide services in the system.